/*!
    \page index.html
    \title OpcUaManager Guide
    \nextpage Introduction and Overview

    \image opcuamanager-logo.png OpcUaManager

    OpcUaManager is a Qt desktop application for browsing, testing, and simulating
    OPC UA servers. It pairs an OPC UA \e client (connect to a server, browse its
    address space, read/write/subscribe to variables, plot trends) with a built-in
    OPC UA \e server studio (design an address space, run a local server, simulate
    values, test security).

    This guide is both a user manual and a developer reference. The first chapters
    explain how to operate the program; the later chapters explain how it is built
    and where each piece of functionality lives in the source code, linking into the
    generated \l {OpcUaManager API Reference}.

    \section1 User guide

    \list
        \li \l {Introduction and Overview} — what the program is and what it is for.
        \li \l {Getting Started} — launch the app, create a project, connect.
        \li \l {OPC UA Client} — connect, browse, read, write, subscribe, trend.
        \li \l {OPC UA Server} — design, configure, run, secure, and simulate a server.
        \li \l {Working with a Server} — end-to-end scenarios through the program.
        \li \l {Configuration} — settings for the app, client, and server.
        \li \l {Troubleshooting} — connection, startup, and configuration problems.
    \endlist

    \section1 Developer guide

    \list
        \li \l {Architecture} — modules, threads, processes, and data flow.
        \li \l {Project Structure} — directories and key source files.
        \li \l {OpcUaManager API Reference} — generated C++ and QML reference.
    \endlist

    \section1 About

    \list
        \li \l {About and Version Information} — application and documentation version.
    \endlist
*/
